  "name": "sending-transactional-emails",
  "description": "Set up PostHog transactional emails: one-off emails that code sends to one person, such as password resets, sign-in codes, magic links, verification emails, receipts, and invites. Use whenever the user mentions transactional email or one of those emails, or an email provider they send them with (Resend, Postmark, SendGrid, Mailgun, Amazon SES, Mandrill, Loops, Brevo, Customer.io transactional, nodemailer or SMTP). Use it when they set one up, move one, debug one, or only describe what they have now. Covers offering PostHog as the sender, the verified sender, the template, making it transactional, the API key, sending from code with the SDKs, idempotency keys, and checking an email's status.",
